From: Vivek Kulkarni <vivek@redwood.ai>
To: Alex Mercer <amercer@launchwave.io>
Cc: Marissa Cole <marissa@redwood.ai>, Ben Carter <ben@redwood.ai>
Date: 2026-11-25T13:30:00-08:00
Subject: Re: Questions on monthly commit ramp for Dec launch

Alex — thanks for the details and the plan. High level proposal below, happy to iterate.

High level approach (proposal):
- Ramp schedule (month-by-month commit):
  • Month 1 (launch month): commit = 50% of projected steady-state monthly tokens + 20% launch grace credit applied to billable usage;
  • Month 2: commit = 100% steady-state;
  • Month 3: commit = 150% steady-state (covers growth window);
- True-up cadence: quarterly true-up with invoice adjustments; immediate reconciliation only if variance exceeds 200% in a single month;
- Surge buffer: automatic short-term burst capacity allowed but billed at overage rate;
- Overage: overages billed at committed per-token discounted rate + 30% premium during first 90 days post-launch, then standard overage thereafter;
- Discounts: per-token discounts tiered by monthly committed volume, applied to committed usage first, then to true-up adjustments;
- One-time launch credit: we can offer a one-time $5k launch credit to offset spike costs if you commit to a 6-month minimum.

I'll put together a short PDF proposal that formalizes the schedule and pricing table. If you want a more generous grace credit or different true-up cadence, flag what matters most.

Regards,
Vivek Kulkarni
Head of Sales, Redwood Inference

Attachment: preliminary MOU (stub)

From: Vivek Kulkarni <vivek@redwood.ai>
To: Marissa Cole <marissa@redwood.ai>, Ben Carter <ben@redwood.ai>, Soojin Lee <soojin@redwood.ai>
Date: 2026-11-27T10:04:00-08:00
Subject: FW: LaunchWave ramp — pricing notes (internal)

Forwarding LaunchWave's plan and my draft. Need alignment on concessions we can make without setting a broad precedent. Key asks from LaunchWave: bigger grace credit, lower overage during first quarter, flexible step-ups. My initial thinking:

- Increase first-month grace credit to 30% (from 20%) if they take a 6-month commit;
- Cap overage premium to 20% (was 30%) for first 60 days;
- Define 'surge' as usage up to 120% of committed for first 30 days before overage applies;
- Make the one-time launch credit contingent on signed MSA and 50% of month 1 commit paid up front;

Marissa/Ben: can you confirm sales OK on concession and if legal can accept the surge definition? Soojin: this will affect CS onboarding and billing notes.

— Vivek

On Nov 25, 2026, Alex Mercer <amercer@launchwave.io> wrote:
> We're closing in on our product launch (targeting early Dec) and need to nail the commit/discount structure...

From: Vivek Kulkarni <vivek@redwood.ai>
To: Alex Mercer <amercer@launchwave.io>, Jamie Liu <j.liu@launchwave.io>
Cc: Marissa Cole <marissa@redwood.ai>, Ben Carter <ben@redwood.ai>, Soojin Lee <soojin@redwood.ai>
Date: 2026-11-29T11:22:00-08:00
Subject: Proposal: launch ramp, true-up, and temporary surge protections

Alex / Jamie — attaching a concise proposal that formalizes the ramp and pricing we discussed. Highlights:

- Ramp schedule (committed monthly tokens):
  • Month 1 (launch): 50% of projected steady-state commit + 30% launch grace credit applied to invoiceable usage;
  • Month 2: 100% steady-state commit;
  • Month 3: 150% steady-state commit;
- Overage policy: for first 60 days post-launch overages billed at committed per-token price + 20% premium; overages thereafter billed at committed price + 40% premium;
- Surge threshold: for day-0 to day-30, usage up to 120% of committed volume will be covered by the surge buffer (no overage charges), after which standard overage rules apply;
- True-up: 60-day true-up window following the quarter in which the usage occurred; adjustments appear on the next billing cycle;
- Credits: one-time $5k launch credit on the first invoice if MSA signed and month 1 invoice 50% pre-paid;
- Minimum term: 6 months to qualify for the launch credit and discounted tiers.

Please review the attached proposal PDF and call out any redlines. If this looks close, we can push to DocuSign next week.

Thanks,
Vivek

Attachment: 20261129-LaunchWave-Proposal.pdf (PDF, 210KB)
